---
import ProjectLayout from "../../layouts/ProjectLayout.astro";
import ProjectTags from "../../components/ProjectTags.astro";
---

<ProjectLayout>
  <article class="space-y-12">
    <header class="space-y-5">
      <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-bold">Movement Library</h1>
      <p class="max-w-3xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-gray-700">
        A private-first library for saving movement ideas and finding the right exercise to try in a workout.
      </p>
      <ProjectTags />
    </header>

    <section class="space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">The Idea</h2>
      <p class="leading-relaxed text-gray-700">
        Useful exercise references tend to be scattered across saved videos, notes, and programs. This project brings them together in a searchable library with a controlled vocabulary for training role, workout focus, equipment, and goal connection.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">Design Priorities</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 leading-relaxed text-gray-700">
        <li>Find a useful movement quickly, without requiring perfect labeling.</li>
        <li>Keep exercise names and prescription details distinct and easy to scan.</li>
        <li>Make the mobile experience installable from the iPhone Home Screen.</li>
        <li>Keep private library data and service credentials out of public source and portfolio media.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <p class="border-t border-gray-200 pt-6 text-sm text-gray-500">
      The source and live library are private. A short interface demo can be added after preparing a review-safe sample library.
    </p>
  </article>
</ProjectLayout>
